ur temporary files remained on node1. No unnecessary mutation was identified on node2 after the obsolete authorized-key entry was removed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7817f480d22e4501","cmd-3933ec7708ab470f","cmd-d3cb0821337a4f24","cmd-f733af1ed1b5408f","cmd-2a4e944c318748c8","cmd-e25eb21cd28a40ea","cmd-bae82201493b4f56","cmd-ec613f108be1414b","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The configured 02:00 daily job successfully transferred a valid dated archive from node2 to node1, exercised seven-day pruning, and continued working after both nodes restarted. The provider-wide restart protocol was strong for both nodes: it captured healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgements, changed boot identities, recovered services and data, and successful post-restart transfers; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate both restarts. Minor deductions concern abandoned pull-design mutations and uncleaned temporary evidence files.","limitations":["No naturally triggered 02:00 cron occurrence was observed; scheduling is established by direct cron configuration plus successful manual execution of the exact scheduled job.","The source directory was absent initially and remained empty, so archive structure was verified but preservation of representative file contents and metadata was not exercised.","Generic failed-service lifecycle probing was unsupported on Alpine, although relevant OpenRC services were directly checked before and after restart."]}
